        }
      ]
    },
    "flow": [
      { "text": "être: who or what you are", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "avoir: what you have", "variant": "verb" },
      { "text": "age and feelings: avoir" }
    ],
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "<strong>être</strong> says who or what you are: name, job, origin, state. <em>Je suis Camille. Elle est infirmière. Nous sommes de Roumanie. Je suis fatigué.</em> After <em>être</em> a job has no article.",
        "tag": "être"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>avoir</strong> says what you have: <em>J'ai deux enfants. Tu as un rendez-vous. Il a une voiture.</em> <em>Je</em> becomes <em>j'</em> before <em>ai</em>.",
        "tag": "avoir"
      },
      {
        "html": "For <strong>age</strong> French uses <strong>avoir</strong>, not être: <em>J'ai 30 ans. Elle a douze ans.</em> Ask: <em>Tu as quel âge ?</em> Not: <em>Je suis 30 ans.</em>",
        "tag": "Age: avoir"
      },
      {
        "html": "Many feelings also use <strong>avoir</strong>: <em>J'ai faim. J'ai soif. J'ai froid. J'ai chaud. J'ai sommeil. J'ai peur.</em> A state like tired or ill uses être: <em>Je suis fatigué.</em>",
        "tag": "avoir + feeling"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>sont</strong> (they are) and <strong>ont</strong> (they have) are different words. With a vowel next to them, <em>ils ont</em> sounds like “eelz-on”: <em>Ils ont un rendez-vous. Ils sont en retard.</em>",
        "tag": "sont or ont?"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>a</strong> (has) has no accent, <strong>à</strong> (at, to) has one: <em>Il a un rendez-vous à 14 h 30.</em> In the same way <em>est</em> (is) is not <em>et</em> (and).",
        "tag": "a or à"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>Je suis 30 ans</em> → ✓ <em>J'ai 30 ans</em>. ✗ <em>Je suis faim</em> → ✓ <em>J'ai faim</em>. ✗ <em>Je ai deux enfants</em> → ✓ <em>J'ai deux enfants</em>. Next: <a href=\"/present-regular\">the present of -er verbs</a> and <a href=\"/present-irregular\">other key irregular verbs</a>.",
    "reference": {
      "showLabel": "Show overview ▼",
      "hideLabel": "Hide overview ▲",
